.TH CJSON_DECLARE_SCOPED 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cjson_declare_scoped \- declare a cjson variable with automatic destruction
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cjson.h>

cjson_declare_scoped(var_name);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Expands to `cjson var_name` decorated with the GCC cleanup attribute so
that cjson_destroy() is called automatically when the variable goes out
of scope.  The variable must be initialized before use (set to NULL or
to a valid node).
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
var_name  Name of the variable to declare.
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
{
    cjson_declare_scoped(root) = cjson_parse("{\e"k\e":1}");
    /* root is freed automatically at the closing brace */
}
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cjson_declare (3),
.BR cjson_destroy (3),
.BR _ccol_destructor (3)
